From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] status: a cellular indicator from the modem's own state

The network indicator draws a modem only while mobile data is the primary
connection, so a phone that is registered without data, searching, or has
no SIM showed nothing cellular.

status/cellular.js reads ModemManager's modems (state, failed reason, SIM,
signal quality, 3GPP registration) and draws one icon whenever the device
has a modem: the signal while it is on a network, no service otherwise,
or no SIM. lumaPresentation/cellularStatus.js maps the state. A searching
modem keeps reporting its last signal, so the signal is drawn only once it
is registered. Without a modem, or without ModemManager, nothing is drawn.

While mobile data is the primary connection the network indicator leaves
the signal to this one.

The no service and no SIM glyphs are Lucide's radio-off and card-sim
(vendor/lucide-shell-status), geometry unchanged, as symbolic strokes at
the status weight.

